# Agent authority & context drift control

**Conflict order:**

1. `docs/project-truth/CONTEXT_BUNDLE.md` + machine-readable `docs/project-truth/*.json` (**vNext.1 current truth**)
2. `DIAL_Consolidated_Plan_v4.md` for non-conflicting detailed product/commercial/architecture requirements
3. `DIAL_Development_Agent_Pack.md`
4. Blueprint / checklists / stitch / WA / promotions / D-53/D-54/D-55/D-61 companions
5. local `.cursor/rules` and skills as enforcement/process
6. current code/runtime state as implementation evidence, **not permission to silently override project truth**

Before material scaffolding or behaviour changes, agents must read `docs/project-truth/CONTEXT_BUNDLE.md`, `project-truth.json`, `feature-registry.json`, and `evidence-registry.json`. Use `.cursor/rules/dial-context-drift.mdc` and `.cursor/skills/dial-context-drift-check/SKILL.md`. Run `pnpm context:check` before merge/sign-off.

**Context drift rule:** if historical prose, code, donor behavior or remembered session context conflicts with vNext.1 truth, do not average them. Current truth wins unless a new explicit decision is approved and the truth/feature/evidence registries are updated in the same work unit.

**Evidence rule:** E1a/E1b/E2a/E3a/E4a and normalized E6a have inherited evidence and begin at Integration Green. Do not repeat their thin-slice stages because of branch/repository migration. E5a and OM-0 begin at Thin Slice Required. Any evidence invalidation requires an explicit record explaining why the previous result is no longer representative.

**Current vNext.1 founder additions:** live credentials never block engineering; integrations must be zero-code key-drop-in; generic AI frontend screens are prohibited; FixItNow is the wholesale Dial a Tech application donor; Dial a Tech adds a pre-award Opportunity Marketplace but post-award converges into the same DIAL Job/Job Reserve workflow; qualified technicians do not pay a per-bid/pay-to-rank toll at launch.

Prefer `.cursor/skills/dial-*` for context drift, money, IDOR/RLS, PspAdapter and high-risk reviews. Catalog: `DIAL_Cursor_Rules_and_Skills.md`. AppSec CI: `DIAL_Security_Toolchain.md` / `dial-security-toolchain.mdc`. v7-2 absorb: `DIAL_v7_2_Adopted_Platform_Extensions.md` (D-53 / D-54) — never the v7 master draft as SoR. External skills: `DIAL_External_Skills_Repos_Utilization.md` (D-55). Plan-phase grill + AI capability merge: Pack §2.2 / D-56. Spare USD browse / ZiG-at-checkout / WA EcoCash+COD buttons: D-57. D-58: agency-only; D-51 owned-stock discarded. D-59: agency FDMS receipt model + in-house Gateway. D-61: Prime is development harness, not product SoR.

**Do not reopen:** C-5 Expo/RN customer shells where native is locked; Baileys/unofficial WA; donor/Google/Mapbox/Fleetbase/Cal.com/Chatwoot/Meili/BI as transaction SoR; second money/job/delivery/catalogue SoR; AI writing payable amounts; informal→B2B visibility; dropping tech WHT; discarded D-51 owned-stock principal; tracer/stub as feature-complete; v7 as SoR; auto-publish checklist/AI without human+evaluation; Command Centre Simulated as live money control; unaudited FX; missing credentials as engineering blocker; repeating accepted slices after migration; generic shared customer storefront skin; cheap FixItNow recreation instead of wholesale port; Opportunity Marketplace becoming a parallel post-award Job/payment system.

For behavioural changes, cite current vNext.1 decision/Feature IDs in PRs and the older D-log section only when it supplies non-conflicting detail. Escalate real conflicts; do not invent another stack.
